34-errors-and-messages: the errors a Python caller meets at the boundary.

Seam: the first line of the messages of the typed boundary, the hint of the
defaulting error, the classes of the exceptions and what a try catches, a
leaked ValueError, the report of the front end without its command line.
Sources: memo A4, A20, A21; catalogue P1, P7, P41, P42, P43, P44, P45; Using
the API, "Typed Expressions" (the error catalogue).  Backends: py, cxx.  Oracle:
none, the goals are Python.

Expected output: MismatchError for length of a Char, ArityError for inc 1 2,
NoInstanceError for succ of a list of functions, ConversionError for None;
each message names the symbol and its scheme (P44).  eval(show) is a
DefaultingError of three lines, with the sentence of the PAKCS REPL and the
hint "state the type: curry.term(goal, type=...)".  The four
typed errors are CurryTypeErrors, which are TypeErrors; EvaluationError and
CompileError are CurryErrors and Exceptions, so "except Exception" and
"except BaseException" both catch an evaluation error (A20).  curry.free('x')
prints its name. CompileError.report holds the front-end report, while
str omits the command line and machine path (A21); the driver prints the
class and the report line "Unexpected end-of-file".  Pins no defect.
